    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Kettle Whistle is a 1997 odds-and-sods compilation by Jane’s Addiction that arrived on Warner Bros. Records during the band’s “Relapse” reunion era. Rather than a standard studio album, it gathers rare and unreleased material, alternate takes, demos, and live recordings, making it a revealing companion piece to the group’s celebrated late-’80s and early-’90s catalog.\n\nThe set’s draw is the mix of archive material and fresh recordings, including the title track and “So What!,” both featuring Flea on bass. With its rough edges, explosive live cuts, and deep-catalog selections, the album functions both as a fan-focused vault release and as a snapshot of Jane’s Addiction’s chemistry at a pivotal moment, earning a reputation as a valuable document of the band’s legacy.",
